System Test Cases
Project: 3D Ultrasound Reconstruction System
Test Case ID: TC-01
Title: Load tracked ultrasound sequence successfully
Pre-conditions:
- The system is installed and launches correctly.
- A valid .mha ultrasound sequence file with tracking metadata is available.
- User has access to the dataset location.

Steps:
1. Launch the application.
2. Select the option to load an ultrasound sequence.
3. Browse to a valid tracked .mha dataset.
4. Open the dataset.

Expected Result:
- The dataset loads without errors.
- Frames and associated metadata are recognized by the system.
- The user can proceed to the next processing step.

Actual Result :
Pass / Fail, plus notes:PASS

Test Case ID: TC-02
Title: Apply fan mask / preprocessing to ultrasound frames
Pre-conditions:
- A valid ultrasound dataset has already been loaded.
- Masking or preprocessing settings are available in the system.

Steps:
1. Load a valid tracked ultrasound dataset.
2. Open the preprocessing or masking interface.
3. Enter or adjust fan mask parameters.
4. Apply the mask to the dataset.
5. Review the processed output frames.

Expected Result:
- The mask is applied successfully to the ultrasound frames.
- Output frames reflect the selected masking or cropping region.
- No crash or corruption occurs during preprocessing.

Actual Result:
Pass / Fail: PASS

